@startuml InvestmentFlow
' Hide the unneeded shadow box for actors
hide footbox

title tawf.finance Investment Flow

actor "Business" as Business
participant "Cooperative" as Coop
participant "Licensed Firm" as Firm
participant "tawf.finance" as Platform
database "Escrow" as Escrow
actor "Investor" as Investor
actor "Retailer" as Retailer

== Phase 1: Deal Origination & Verification ==

Business -> Coop : Submits Purchase Order (PO)
note right of Business
  Local business (warung, farm)
  needs capital for goods
end note

Coop -> Coop : Verifies business & deal
note right of Coop
  Cooperative knows businesses
  personally, validates on ground
end note

Coop -> Firm : Requests verification
Firm -> Firm : Issues investment instrument
note right of Firm
  Licensed financial firm
  holds regulatory license
end note

== Phase 2: Investment Creation ==

Firm -> Platform : Confirms deal
Platform -> Platform : Creates digital receipt
note right of Platform
  On-chain record tying
  investment to specific PO
end note

Platform -> Escrow : **Locks funds in escrow**

Escrow -> Investor : **Opens investment opportunity**

== Phase 3: Investment ==

Investor -> Escrow : Invests ($10 minimum)
note right of Investor
  Halal returns from
  real trade, 8-18% APY
end note

Escrow -> Business : Releases capital
Business -> Business : Purchases inventory

== Phase 4: Fulfillment & Repayment ==

Business -> Retailer : Delivers goods
Retailer -> Business : Pays for goods

Business -> Escrow : Repays principal + profit
note right of Business
  30-90 day deal duration
end note

Escrow -> Investor : **Returns investment + profit**

@enduml
